When a model scores answers at 80%, are about 80% right?
Recorded answers on the 2,198 questions. Each dot is a group of answers with similar confidence: its average confidence (x) against the share right (y). Above
the diagonal, the model was right more often than its confidence says; below it, less often. Dot size: • 20 to 199 answers, ● 200 or more. Groups with fewer
than 20 answers are left out of the plot (the table keeps them).

